# SEC-01 (27 Aug 2026): these are real, live application databases -- they
# accumulate password hashes, refresh-token hashes, encrypted BYOK keys and
# MFA secrets, and real tenant/ledger data as the app is used. None of that
# belongs in version control at any point, hashed/encrypted or not. Added
# here after finding backend/eivanta.duckdb and backend/eivanta_core.db
# were BOTH already tracked (committed locally, never yet pushed to
# origin) -- see the founder-facing note this session left about untracking
# them and why the commit that added them still needs a deliberate,
# explicit decision before this repo is ever pushed.
*.duckdb
backend/eivanta_core.db

# 2 Sep 2026: *.duckdb doesn't match DuckDB's own write-ahead-log file
# (<name>.duckdb.wal) -- found backend/eivanta.duckdb.wal sitting untracked
# and about to be swept into a commit for this (public) repo before this
# was added. Same live-data reasoning as the block above.
*.duckdb.wal

# OPS-03 (3 Sep 2026): backend/backup.py's real encrypted backups land
# here by default (EIVANTA_BACKUP_DIR, defaults to backend/backups/).
# Same live-data reasoning as the *.duckdb block above -- an encrypted
# backup is still a full copy of every password hash, refresh-token
# hash, and tenant's BYOK ciphertext in the platform, and belongs in a
# real backup location, never in version control.
backend/backups/

# OPS-05 (3 Sep 2026): backend/status.py's real, togglable maintenance-mode
# flag file. Purely an operational runtime toggle an operator creates and
# removes directly on the host (or via the EIVANTA_MAINTENANCE_MODE env var)
# -- never source, never intended for version control.
backend/.maintenance_mode

# Session scratch/cleanup staging directories -- never intended for the
# repo; the files inside were moved here pending manual deletion by the
# founder, not to be committed.
_to_delete/
